KW  - Information systems
KW  - Reef restoration
AB  - As environmental modelling outputs increasingly inform decisions, careful management of their provenance supports transparency and scientific integrity. Provena is a system designed to capture this provenance and provide traceability across modelling activities, from datasets and models through to the organisations and people involved. Originally developed for the Reef Restoration and Adaptation Program (RRAP) to support the Modelling and Decision Support (MDS) subprogram, Provena underpins the MDS information system and facilitates the management of ecological and environmental model outputs and collaboration across teams. Operational use of the system has revealed new needs, including tracking studies that span multiple modelling activities and managing versions of data over time. These insights have driven the development of Provena 2.0. In this paper, we outline these new features, including tools to register studies linking related model runs and mechanisms for versioning datasets and registry items to track changes over time. Together, these features improve traceability and defensibility of modelling artefacts and support reproducibility.
