KW  - Landscape connectivity
KW  - Habitat fragmentation
KW  - Conservation planning
KW  - R package
KW  - Protected areas
KW  - Habitat availability metrics
AB  - Habitat fragmentation and climate change threaten biodiversity, emphasizing the need for landscape connectivity to help species access habitat resources and track ongoing shifts in suitable areas. Given limited conservation funds and land-use conflicts, the efficient prioritization of connectivity measures is essential. To that end, we developed the Makurhini R package, an open-source tool for systematically calculating key fragmentation and connectivity metrics. Makurhini provides integrated analytical capabilities and efficiently processes large datasets, including parallel processing, allowing parameterization for different species and landscape contexts. Key features include characterizing links using Euclidean, least-cost, and circuit theory approaches; calculating the Probability of Connectivity, Equivalent Connected Area, and Protected Connected indicators, among other metrics; and ranking nodes and links by their contribution to connectivity. Case studies in Mexico, Colombia, and Spain demonstrate its applicability. Makurhini provides a robust framework to deliver ecologically and policy-relevant connectivity and fragmentation metrics for conservation and restoration in fragmented landscapes.
ER  - 
